				"string" : "## Registration\n\n`addOns addStyler: ElixirFunctionExpanderStyler new` in {{gtMethod:name=GtElixirCoderModel>>initializeAddOns:}}. Composite styler runs it on text changes."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-25T14:34:26.175976+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-07-20T16:07:26.167822+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "4X+pIufdQPigSJcswMh0VA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## BEAM-side\n\n`GtBridge.Analysis.call_sites/2` parses the AST, resolves aliases (using the context module's preamble when missing from source), filters unresolvable / unsourced / non-existent calls, and returns `[%{target_module, function, arity, line, column}]`.\n\nThe styler does not call that one. It calls `GtBridge.Analysis.call_sites_relation/2`, which is the same data handed through `JSON.encode!`, and it decodes the result locally with `STONJSON`. That one detail is the difference between a 17ms restyle and a 739ms one, so it gets its own section below."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-07-20T16:07:36.35456+08:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-07-20T16:14:19.112663+08:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "n7wTRLDkTCy2DU7k+ZPAjQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Everything compound that crosses the bridge arrives as a lazy handle, and every field you read off a handle is an HTTP round trip to `GtBridge.ObjectRegistry.get_attribute`. Scalars are the exception: an Elixir integer arrives as a real `SmallInteger`, a string as a `ByteString`.\n\nSo the boundary is value-preserving for scalars and handle-based for containers. Encoding to JSON turns a container back into a scalar, which is the only way to carry structured data across as values. After `STONJSON` decodes it, the line and column numbers are ordinary Smalltalk integers built locally, never fetched.\n\nEvaluate this to watch each shape land:"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "pharoSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-07-20T16:07:43.342712+08:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-07-20T16:07:43.342712+08:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "9v+oXcGORVyCHDl7GcDpQA=="
							},
							"code" : "| app probe |\napp := BeamLinkApplication uniqueInstance.\nprobe := [ :expr | expr -> (app evaluateAndWait: expr) class name ].\n{ probe value: '42'.\n  probe value: '\"a string\"'.\n  probe value: '[1, 2, 3]'.\n  probe value: '%{a: 1}'.\n  probe value: 'JSON.encode!(%{a: 1})' }"
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
