				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Why the relation crosses as a String\n"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-07-20T16:07:53.629661+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-07-20T16:07:53.629661+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "mHzKMysPTvGsE2fcHO0chg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## What it cost before\n\nThe styler reads all five fields of every call site on every keystroke. As handles that is one round trip per field: 113 sites by 5 fields is 565 round trips at roughly 1.34ms each.\n\nMeasured on a 535-line file:\n\n- cold style: 922ms, now 73ms\n- warm restyle: 739ms, now 17ms\n\nThe `cachedHash` / `cachedSites` cache did not rescue this, because it cached the handles rather than their values. A warm restyle re-fetched every field and still paid nearly the full price.\n\nWorth contrasting with the wrench half of this same styler, which was built cost-first a day later: it walks the SmaCC AST locally and asks the BEAM one batched question, so after warm-up its bridge traffic is zero. Same file, same styler, two different eras of thinking. See the \"Wrench: Unresolved Module Affordance\" page.\n\nNote that the styler now requires a gt_bridge providing `call_sites_relation/2`. An image updated ahead of its project's hex pin will get a `BeamBridgeEvalError` back; the styler skips the cache write in that case so it retries on the next restyle rather than staying blank."
			}
		]
	},
